  "obligation": "Execute all integer atomic load/store, RMW arithmetic/bitwise/exchange/compare-exchange widths and memory-independent fences through the shared VM, with natural alignment, unsigned narrow reads, wrapped narrow compares/stores and sequential consistency.",
  "representation": "One flat Rust table owns 63 operator-to-kind/load/store mappings and derives selectors, decoder admission, input arity, value type and disassembly. Atomic access composes existing scalar memory reads/writes and I64 integer rules; narrow wrapping derives from byte width. One existing backing lock spans the entire access/RMW. A single ordering mutex is acquired before backing locks for atomic access, memory length/size and growth; fences join that order and perform a native SeqCst fence. Lock granularity is a correctness choice, not a performance claim. Original memory sharedness is preserved; access operators also admit unshared memory. No new memory representation, VM, executor, side identity map or suite-dependent production path.",
  "lowering": "WasmAtomicAccess has a complete register window containing memory, effective u64 address and operation-specific values; arity derives from named AtomicInput roles and operation kind. Guest operands remain reserved while the window is built. Generic validation rejects unknown selectors and wrong window counts before effects; liveness derives every pending root from the operand layout. Load/store/RMW input types decode before acquiring locks; result encoding occurs after guards are released. Alignment is checked before scalar bounds admission, matching Node when both conditions fail.",
  "scope": "The previous 92 affected pinned files cover integer/vector memory, bulk/data, growth, imports/exports/linking/start, array data segments and threads/custom-page-sizes. No full suite.",
